{"format":"bench-library","formatVersion":1,"id":"keypad","name":"Keypads","version":"1.0.0","author":"Bench Workshop","owner":"codeopen0-cpu","description":"Membrane keypads (4x4 and 4x3): each key joins its row wire to its column wire while it's held, exactly as the real ones do. Press the keys in the run panel. Includes Keypad.h.","category":"Input","needsApp":"0.3.0","code":"// A membrane keypad: a grid of switches. Holding a key joins its row wire to its column wire\n// (nothing else: no power, no chip). A board finds the key by driving one wire low at a time and\n// reading which of the others follows (Keypad.h does that).\nbench.device('keypad', (part) => {\n  const keys = part.control('keys');\n  const screen = part.screen('keys');\n  const cols = screen.cols, rows = screen.rows;\n  const labels = cols === 4 ? ['1', '2', '3', 'A', '4', '5', '6', 'B', '7', '8', '9', 'C', '*', '0', '#', 'D'] : ['1', '2', '3', '4', '5', '6', '7', '8', '9', '*', '0', '#'];\n  let held = [];\n  return {\n    step(io) {\n      held = keys.down;\n      for (let i = 0; i < labels.length; i++) {\n        const r = Math.floor(i / cols), c = i % cols;\n        const down = held.includes(labels[i]);\n        io.connect(`R${r + 1}`, `C${c + 1}`, down);\n        screen.set(c, r, down ? 1 : 0);\n      }\n    },\n    status() {\n      return [held.length ? `holding ${held.join(' ')}` : 'no key held'];\n    },\n  };\n});\n","sketch":{"Keypad.h":{"classes":["Keypad"],"exports":["makeKeymap","NO_KEY","IDLE","PRESSED","HOLD","RELEASED"],"code":"// Keypad.h (Mark Stanley & Alexander Brevig's library), the usual parts: getKey(), getKeys(),\n// waitForKey(), getState(), isPressed(), setDebounceTime(), setHoldTime(), addEventListener().\n// It scans like the real one: one column driven low at a time, rows read with pull-ups.\nconst NO_KEY = 0; // (C's '\\0': \"if (key)\" is false for it)\nconst IDLE = 0, PRESSED = 1, HOLD = 2, RELEASED = 3;\n/** the keymap as one list (the C++ macro just hands over the array) */\nfunction makeKeymap(k) { return Array.isArray(k[0]) ? k.flat() : k; }\n\nclass Keypad {\n  constructor(map, rowPins, colPins, rows, cols) {\n    this.map = makeKeymap(map);\n    this.rowPins = Array.from(rowPins).slice(0, rows);\n    this.colPins = Array.from(colPins).slice(0, cols);\n    this.rows = rows;\n    this.cols = cols;\n    this.debounce = 10;\n    this.holdTime = 500;\n    this.lastScan = -1e9;\n    this.state = IDLE;\n    this.key = NO_KEY;\n    this.pressedAt = 0;\n    this.listener = null;\n    this.down = new Set();\n    this.keyStates = new Map(); // char -> state (for getKeys / isPressed)\n    for (const r of this.rowPins) pinMode(r, INPUT_PULLUP);\n    for (const c of this.colPins) pinMode(c, INPUT_PULLUP);\n  }\n  begin(map) { this.map = makeKeymap(map); }\n  setDebounceTime(ms) { this.debounce = Math.max(1, ms); }\n  setHoldTime(ms) { this.holdTime = ms; }\n  addEventListener(fn) { this.listener = fn; }\n  /** which keys are down now: drive each column low in turn, read the rows */\n  scan() {\n    const now = new Set();\n    for (const r of this.rowPins) pinMode(r, INPUT_PULLUP);\n    for (let c = 0; c < this.cols; c++) {\n      const cp = this.colPins[c];\n      pinMode(cp, OUTPUT);\n      digitalWrite(cp, LOW);\n      delay(5); // (the simulation needs a step to see the column go low: a real one needs microseconds)\n      for (let r = 0; r < this.rows; r++) if (digitalRead(this.rowPins[r]) === LOW) now.add(this.map[r * this.cols + c]);\n      digitalWrite(cp, HIGH);\n      pinMode(cp, INPUT_PULLUP); // (resting: held high, not left floating)\n    }\n    return now;\n  }\n  /** the key just pressed, or NO_KEY */\n  getKey() {\n    if (millis() - this.lastScan < this.debounce) return NO_KEY;\n    this.lastScan = millis();\n    const now = this.scan();\n    let pressed = NO_KEY;\n    for (const k of now) if (!this.down.has(k)) { pressed = k; this.setState(k, PRESSED); }\n    for (const k of this.down) if (!now.has(k)) this.setState(k, RELEASED);\n    for (const k of now) if (this.down.has(k) && this.keyStates.get(k) === PRESSED && millis() - this.pressedAt > this.holdTime) this.setState(k, HOLD);\n    if (pressed !== NO_KEY) this.pressedAt = millis();\n    this.down = now;\n    if (!now.size && this.state === RELEASED) this.state = IDLE;\n    return pressed;\n  }\n  setState(k, s) {\n    this.keyStates.set(k, s);\n    this.key = k;\n    this.state = s;\n    if (s === RELEASED) this.keyStates.set(k, IDLE);\n    if (this.listener) this.listener(k);\n  }\n  getKeys() { this.getKey(); return this.down.size > 0; }\n  isPressed(k) { return this.down.has(k); }\n  getState() { return this.state; }\n  keyStateChanged() { return true; }\n  waitForKey() {\n    for (;;) {\n      const k = this.getKey();\n      if (k !== NO_KEY) return k;\n      delay(1);\n    }\n  }\n}\n"}},"parts":[{"id":"keypad4x4","name":"Keypad 4x4","description":"16 keys: 1-9, 0, A-D, * and #. 8 wires: R1-R4 (rows) and C1-C4 (columns), left to right on its ribbon. Press its keys in the run panel while running. Keypad keypad = Keypad(makeKeymap(keys), rowPins, colPins, 4, 4);","swatch":"#2a2c31","mass":8,"shape":[{"box":[6.9,0.08,7.6],"at":[0,0.04,0],"color":"#2a2c31"},{"screen":{"id":"keys","size":[6.4,6.4],"px":[4,4],"mode":"pixels","on":"#4f9cff","off":"#e6e8ee","bg":"#2a2c31","dots":true},"at":[0,0.09,0.3]},{"box":[2.2,0.03,2.4],"at":[0,0.015,-4.9],"color":"#cfd3da","collide":false}],"pinRows":[{"ids":["R1","R2","R3","R4","C1","C2","C3","C4"],"at":[-0.889,0,-6.2],"kinds":{"R1":"out","R2":"out","R3":"out","R4":"out","C1":"out","C2":"out","C3":"out","C4":"out"}}],"controls":[{"id":"keys","kind":"keys","label":"Keys","cols":4,"keys":["1","2","3","A","4","5","6","B","7","8","9","C","*","0","#","D"]}],"device":"keypad"},{"id":"keypad4x3","name":"Keypad 4x3","description":"12 keys like a phone: 1-9, *, 0, #. 7 wires: R1-R4 and C1-C3. Press its keys in the run panel while running.","swatch":"#2a2c31","mass":6,"shape":[{"box":[5.2,0.08,7.6],"at":[0,0.04,0],"color":"#2a2c31"},{"screen":{"id":"keys","size":[4.8,6.4],"px":[3,4],"mode":"pixels","on":"#4f9cff","off":"#e6e8ee","bg":"#2a2c31","dots":true},"at":[0,0.09,0.3]}],"pinRows":[{"ids":["R1","R2","R3","R4","C1","C2","C3"],"at":[-0.762,0,-6.2],"kinds":{"R1":"out","R2":"out","R3":"out","R4":"out","C1":"out","C2":"out","C3":"out"}}],"controls":[{"id":"keys","kind":"keys","label":"Keys","cols":3,"keys":["1","2","3","4","5","6","7","8","9","*","0","#"]}],"device":"keypad"}],"examples":[{"name":"Keypad to serial","description":"A 4x4 keypad on 8 pins: every key you press in the run panel is printed in the serial monitor.","project":{"format":"bench-workshop","version":1,"name":"Keypad to serial","parts":[{"uid":"board","type":"maker-board","name":"Board","params":{"usb":true},"parent":null,"pos":[-6,0,-6],"rot":[0,0,0,1]},{"uid":"pad","type":"keypad/keypad4x4","name":"Keypad","params":{},"parent":null,"pos":[6,0,2],"rot":[0,0,0,1]}],"wires":[{"id":"w1","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"GP9"},"b":{"uid":"pad","pin":"R1"},"color":"#e04848"},{"id":"w2","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"GP8"},"b":{"uid":"pad","pin":"R2"},"color":"#f08c2a"},{"id":"w3","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"GP7"},"b":{"uid":"pad","pin":"R3"},"color":"#e8c547"},{"id":"w4","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"GP6"},"b":{"uid":"pad","pin":"R4"},"color":"#3fbf7f"},{"id":"w5","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"GP5"},"b":{"uid":"pad","pin":"C1"},"color":"#4f9cff"},{"id":"w6","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"GP4"},"b":{"uid":"pad","pin":"C2"},"color":"#9b59d6"},{"id":"w7","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"GP3"},"b":{"uid":"pad","pin":"C3"},"color":"#9aa1b2"},{"id":"w8","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"GP2"},"b":{"uid":"pad","pin":"C4"},"color":"#f2f2f2"}],"programs":{"board":{"lang":"arduino","source":"// Which key? Press keys in the run panel (select the keypad's card on the right).\n#include <Keypad.h>\n\nconst byte ROWS = 4;\nconst byte COLS = 4;\nchar keys[ROWS][COLS] = {\n  {'1', '2', '3', 'A'},\n  {'4', '5', '6', 'B'},\n  {'7', '8', '9', 'C'},\n  {'*', '0', '#', 'D'}\n};\nbyte rowPins[ROWS] = {9, 8, 7, 6};   // R1-R4\nbyte colPins[COLS] = {5, 4, 3, 2};   // C1-C4\n\nKeypad keypad = Keypad(makeKeymap(keys), rowPins, colPins, ROWS, COLS);\n\nvoid setup() {\n  Serial.begin(115200);\n  Serial.println(\"Press a key\");\n}\n\nvoid loop() {\n  char key = keypad.getKey();\n  if (key) {\n    Serial.print(\"key: \");\n    Serial.println(key);\n  }\n}\n"}},"boards":[]}}]}